{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/940040-mussughana-the-ravenous-swarm-2e","id":940040,"title":"Mussughana, The Ravenous Swarm (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-30T04:18:04-07:00","id":940040,"title":"Mussughana, The Ravenous Swarm (2E)","content":"In the beginning, there was only hunger. Before the world was born, it existed, howling madly for sustenance against the infinite void of pre-being. According to those who worship it, Mussughana was born before Creation itself, the very conceptual spirit of the emptiness of pure, unbridled entropy. It is older than Father Wolf, older than Mother Luna, perhaps even older than Helios. The Worm That Feasts was at peace only when it had nothing to devour \u2014 at the instant of creation, its serene existence was shattered, hurled into madness by the variety of forms and structures vomited forth from the heart of all existence. Only when all that is has been returned to the primordial chaos of all that was can Mussughana once more know peace.<br /> <br /> Although it coalesced into a fixed form decades ago, that fixed form is not a single, discrete entity. Mussughana takes the form of a vast swarm of crawling, writhing, buzzing things with an amalgamation of traits insectoid, piscine and even mammalian, along with creatures far stranger than any the earth has ever seen. The swarm varies in size, depending upon how well it has fed (see the Ravenous Hunger power at the end of this section): from a radius of five yards in its \u201cnormal\u201d state, up to 15 miles in radius in the largest feeding frenzy recorded by the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> [For more information on this Idigam, see p. 147 of Night Horrors: Wolfsbane]<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Mussughana, The Ravenous Swarm</b></u><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 5<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 12, Finesse 15, Resistance 10<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Hunger 4, Despair 3, Disease 2<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Discorporate, Fetter, Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Drain, Gauntlet Vision, Essence Thief, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/480962-ephemeral-being-house-rules-new-epic-numen\">Legion</a>, Seek, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/626202-new-numina\">Sever Fetter</a>, Speed, Four Influence dots<br /> <b>Essence Shaping:</b> Essence Attack, Essence Void, Forge Servant (Claimed, Spawn), Locus Manipulation, One Million Eyes<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Beastmaster, Call Void Spirit, Devourer, Ravenous Hunger, Venomous Ichor<br /> <br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 35<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 100<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> See Ravenous Hunger<br /> <b>Speed: </b>27<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 25<br /> <br /> <b>Ban: </b>If an offering of food is placed before it, Mussughana stops all activity to devour it,.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Pure, pottable water<br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Ravenous Hunger:</b> Mussughana does not lose Essence as other idigam do. The more it consumes, the more it hunger grows, and this hunger is represented by its Essence expenditure, and its consumption by its Size. As long as Mussughana has less than 15 Essence, it follows the standard rules for idigam as described on p. 132 of this book. At this level, the spirit is a swarm equal to five yards in radius. As the spirit\u2019s Essence pool grows, so, too, does its Size \u2014 but along with its greater power comes a greater hunger. Eventually, the spirit runs out of sustenance and collapses back to its smallest size.<br /> <br /> The following table shows its Size and Essence expenditure per day based on current Essence. <hr /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Essence Pool</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Size / Swarm Radius</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Essence Per Day</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1 to 15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">16 to 25</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">26 to 35</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">20 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">36 to 45</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">40 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">46 to 55</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">80 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">56 to 65</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">160 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">66 to 75</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">320 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">76 to 85</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">640 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">86 to 95</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1,280 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">96 to 100</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2,560 Yards</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_li